1-- P1 — Duplicate manifest records are marked invalid, but `_ov_obs_prior_record` ignores `_BASELINE_INVALID` and treats the retained first row as trusted ownership ([scripts/upgrade.sh:990](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:990), [scripts/upgrade.sh:1840](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:1840)). A duplicate `SPEC/v1/*` row therefore authorizes the forced delete-and-replace path at [scripts/upgrade.sh:2040](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:2040), violating fail-closed provenance handling.
2-
3-- P1 — Downgrading with `--pin` to a pre-marker release drops marker ownership and claims the fallback `VERSION` reflects the pin ([scripts/upgrade.sh:2131](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:2131)). The same script explicitly never updates root `VERSION` ([scripts/upgrade.sh:346](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:346)), so a downgraded installation reports its stale install-time version, breaking update and forensic version state.
4-
5:- P2 — An owned but emptied `SPEC/v1` loses ownership on an install rerun: continuity is asserted at [scripts/install.sh:2334](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/install.sh:2334), but the generator emits only files or symlinks and cannot serialize an empty directory ([scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:178](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:178)). Subsequent upgrades misclassify the contract as an adopter fork and leave it empty.
6-
7-The pure ownership oracle and shell syntax pass, but they do not cover these stateful provenance and pin transitions. The duplicate-record path can authorize replacement from explicitly ambiguous input, while the pin path deterministically publishes the wrong installed version; both make rc.2 unsafe to cut.
8-
