- Payloads redigidos + diffs + `PROVENANCE-ga.md` + `MANIFEST-ga.sha256` neste diretório.
- Nenhum commit feito nesta sessão (autorização do Owner pendente para as curas).
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round19.txt:9:   **Minimal fix:** hash each input before invoking Codex, verify those hashes immediately afterward and again before aggregation, and include per-part input manifests in `MANIFEST-ga.sha256`.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round19.txt:16:   The RC positive-control receipt is selected only by `headSha`. Another tag pointing at the same commit can supply a successful `Await release-gate` job while the actual rc.3 npm waiter is failed or absent, falsely satisfying the prerequisite used by the GA ceremony. The later release/npm monitors repeat the SHA-only selection.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round21.txt:6:Concrete failure: commit 1 stages `W3-approved-draft.md`, the staged-W3 manifest/baseline, and ancillary cure-rail files without an external content pin. The ceremony manifest verified at line 157 covers only nine PLAN-166 ceremony files. An accidental edit to the W3 draft—or a stale, self-consistent W3 pack plus regenerated manifest—passes G0 and becomes part of `parent_sha`, beyond visibility of the later delta guard.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round21.txt:10:Concrete failure: neither ceremony rechecks the remote tag object after the release workflows finish. If the remote tag is deleted or force-moved after the npm tag-liveness check succeeds, the old workflow receipts and GitHub Release remain selectable; GA’s final check covers only `origin/main`, so it can announce a release whose remote tag now points elsewhere.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round21.txt:11:Minimal fix: immediately before success, take one `git ls-remote` snapshot of the plain and peeled tag refs and require exact equality with the locally verified tag object and commit.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round23.txt:3:Concrete failure scenario: `BASE_TAG="v1.2.0"` is never bound to an immutable commit/tag object or checked against `origin`. A stale or mistakenly moved local tag makes the runner review the wrong diff while every hash, manifest, timestamp, and verdict remains internally consistent. `PROVENANCE-ga.md` records only the symbolic base name, and `validate_ga_evidence` validates only the RC SHA, so the wrong evidence can be reused and signed for GA.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round23.txt:5:Minimal fix: pin the expected v1.2.0 tag object and peeled commit; fail closed on local signature and a single `ls-remote` plain/peeled comparison; record both SHAs in provenance and validate them on reuse.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round14.txt:2:   The remote-tag checks accept a matching peeled commit instead of requiring the exact signed tag object. Deleting and recreating RC3 or GA as a lightweight/different annotated tag at the same commit therefore passes. In `MONITOR_ONLY`, old workflow runs selected only by `headSha` can then be reused while signing and pre-push verification are skipped. Minimal fix: from one `ls-remote` snapshot, require the plain remote ref to equal the local signed tag object, the peeled ref to equal its commit, and verify `git tag -v` for both RC and GA tags.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round18.txt:1:P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:110` and `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:581` — `release.yml` can publish the rc.3 pre-release before the RC script checks the `await-release-gate` positive control. If that job fails or the monitor times out, RC3-CUT aborts but leaves the signed remote tag, public pre-release, and `publishedAt`. After 24 hours, GA-CUT accepts exactly that state without rechecking the failed control and can promote. Minimal fix: GA G0 must locate the `npm-publish.yml` run for the exact `RC_TAG` and `RC_SHA` and require its `Await release-gate` job to have concluded `success`; alternatively, RC3-CUT must draft the pre-release on control failure and GA must require a durable success receipt.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round5.txt:5:- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:78`, `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:147` — Authorization decisions depend on mutable control files outside the signed manifest sets. RC3 selects the authoritative round from `RAIL-STATUS.txt`; GA reuses evidence based on `PROVENANCE-ga.md`, while `run-ga-repass.sh:185` excludes provenance from `MANIFEST-ga.sha256`. An edited status can select an earlier GO, or stale internally consistent evidence can be paired with rewritten provenance and reused. If these files are already in the manifests, the templates instead fail guard set equality because they omit them. Minimal fix: manifest a machine-readable final-status/anchor record and verify manifest content and exact set before either GO selection or reuse.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round27.txt:18:Concrete failure scenario: validate receipt selection filters only by `headSha`. A successful `pull_request` run for the same SHA can be selected while the required `push`/`main` run is delayed, absent, or later fails. The script can consequently push the release tag without a successful main-push validation receipt.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round6.txt:1:- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:100` — Cure evidence and the staged pack are verified independently. `MANIFEST-cures.sha256` covers only round tuples; `PROVENANCE-cures.md` is merely allowed on disk, and G0 never checks that it names `EXPECTED_HEAD` or pins the current `staged-rc3/{MANIFEST,BASELINE}.sha256`. A stale GO evidence directory plus a different self-consistent pack therefore passes and is signed as reviewed. Minimal fix: record both pack-manifest hashes and the exact anchor in provenance, include provenance in `MANIFEST-cures.sha256`, and compare those fields exactly in G0.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round26.txt:7:- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:668` — The script undrafts the GA before checking that the RC tag, GA tag object, and `origin/main` remain coherent. If the GA tag moves after the npm liveness check, or main rolls back during the npm wait, the release becomes public and only then the later checks abort, leaving the inconsistent GA public. Minimal fix: perform all remote-ref/main checks before undrafting, verify the resulting public state, and automatically re-draft if any post-undraft recheck fails.

