.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round20.txt:6:Concrete failure: interruption while `shasum` writes directly to `MANIFEST-ga.sha256` can leave a valid partial manifest after `RUNNER-OVERALL: rc=0` was recorded. On rerun, `validate_ga_evidence` checks only the listed hashes; it does not require exactly the expected 11 basenames. It reuses and commits the partial evidence, and the delta guard rejects only after the verdict commit, leaving a non-rerunnable state.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round20.txt:10:Concrete failure: `MONITOR_ONLY=1` does not prevent the evidence runner and commit-1 phase. After a post-tag monitoring timeout, an accidental local truncation of an evidence file makes validation rerun Codex and commit new evidence, moving HEAD beyond the already-pushed tag. The script then skips verdict/CI/tag creation, monitors the old tag, and declares GA with an untagged, unpushed local HEAD—the subsequent W3 instructions anchor the wrong commit.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round29.txt:1:P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:174,202` — Script-review selection derives the final verdict from the highest round number, but binds the current ceremony manifest only to the last unnumbered `CEREMONY-MANIFEST-SHA256-AT-REVIEW` provenance line. A stale higher-numbered GO can therefore be combined with a newer lower-numbered NO-GO or interrupted review; all manifests, tuple checks, and the current-manifest comparison still pass. Minimal fix: record and verify the ceremony-manifest hash for `SFINAL_N` specifically, require `SFINAL_N >= 5`, and enforce exact manifest equality with the expected round tuples plus provenance.
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-rc3-scripts/verdict-cures-round10.txt:3:P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:155`: G0 accepts dirty `$VF`, `$VF.asc`, and `$VD` without rejecting symlinks or other non-regular files. A pre-existing `$VD` symlink to `$VF` causes the verdict-template redirection at line 297 to overwrite the already-signed verdict-fields file. Both paths are then staged, while local and server-side readers follow the symlink; because the embedded signature is only checked for presence server-side, the invalid signature binding can pass and reach release. Minimal fix: reject symlinks/non-regular partial artifacts, generate VF/VD through same-directory temporary regular files plus atomic rename, assert both are regular immediately before staging, and re-run `gpg --verify "$VF.asc" "$VF"` after generating VD but before moving the signature.
