.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-r2/transcript-c.log:13421:- **P1 — A negative verdict can authorize the release.** The new guard parses the YAML but never checks `fields["verdict"]`; it begins enforcement with `release_tag` at [.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py:285](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py:285). Thus `verdict: NO-GO`, an unknown value, or a missing verdict receives the same decision as `GO` when the remaining fields are valid. The driver then signs the tag at [.claude/scripts/local/release.sh:630](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/.claude/scripts/local/release.sh:630). The downstream pair-rail validator also does not inspect the verdict value, so `release-gate` can succeed and the new poller can grant npm publication despite a cross-model NO-GO. Require an explicitly release-authorizing verdict—normally exact `GO`—before accepting the delta or signing.
